Let me also check that the PHP visibility test is correct. The original PHP logic was:
```rust
let is_pub = line.trim_start().starts_with("public")
    || !line.trim_start().starts_with("private")
        && !line.trim_start().starts_with("protected");
```

This is equivalent to: `starts_with("public") || (!starts_with("private") && !starts_with("protected")) which due to operator precedence is: starts_with("public") || ((!starts_with("private")) && (!starts_with("protected")))`.

For a function with no visibility modifier (like `function helper_function($x)), this evaluates to: false || (true && true) = true`. So it's public.
For `private function validate($data): false || (false && true) = false`. So it's private.
For `public function index(): true || ... = true`. So it's public.

My `NotPrivateOrProtected rule computes: !starts_with("private") && !starts_with("protected")` which for:
• No modifier: true && true = true ✓
• private ...: false && true = false ✓ 
• public ...: true && true = true ✓

